meta {
  name: Match Group
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/student/group-finder/match
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{studentAccessToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "preferred_city": "Bangalore",
    "friends": [
      {
        "name": "Alex",
        "course_id": "{{courseMasterId}}"
      },
      {
        "name": "Sara",
        "course_id": "{{courseMasterId2}}"
      }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  Finds colleges/institution-groups that can satisfy every friend's chosen
  course, optionally narrowed to a preferred city/state. 2-6 friends per
  request.

  Each friend picks one `course_id` (a CourseMaster / platform course
  catalog entry, e.g. "B.Tech Computer Science Engineering" — from
  GET /student/group-finder/courses?search=). That course's Discipline is
  always used as a match criterion; its Study Level is used too only if
  the catalog entry has one set (Study Level is optional on CourseMaster).
  Stream is never taken as separate input — it's implied by the
  Discipline. 404 if any friend's course_id doesn't resolve to a real
  catalog entry.

  The "match unit" is an institution group (e.g. "M.S. Ramaiah Group"),
  not a single college — two friends can be satisfied by DIFFERENT
  sub-colleges within the same group (one friend's engineering course at
  Institute A, another friend's arts course at Institute B, same parent
  group). A standalone college with no group is treated as its own
  singleton group.

  Response `data`:
  {
    "fullyMatched": [
      {
        "groupId": "ING-1" | null,
        "groupName": "M.S. Ramaiah Group",
        "city": "Bangalore",
        "state": "Karnataka",
        "matchedFriendCount": 2,
        "totalFriendCount": 2,
        "isFullyMatched": true,
        "matches": [
          {
            "friendName": "Alex",
            "collegeId": "CLG-1",
            "collegeName": "Ramaiah Inst. of Tech",
            "courseId": "CRS-1",
            "courseName": "B.E. Computer Science",
            "courseCode": "BECS",
            "studyLevelName": "B.Tech",
            "disciplineName": "Computer Science Engineering",
            "availability": "high",
            "availabilityLabel": "High Availability",
            "availableSpecializations": [
              { "courseId": "CRS-1", "disciplineId": "DIS-1", "disciplineName": "Computer Science Engineering", "courseName": "B.E. Computer Science" },
              { "courseId": "CRS-2", "disciplineId": "DIS-2", "disciplineName": "Mechanical Engineering", "courseName": "B.E. Mechanical" }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "unmatchedFriendNames": []
      }
    ],
    "partiallyMatched": [ /* same shape, isFullyMatched: false, unmatchedFriendNames non-empty */ ]
  }

  `availability` is derived from live seat data (CourseQuotaSeats under the
  college's currently-open admission cycle) — "high" (>30% seats open),
  "limited" (some seats open, ≤30%), "waitlist" (0 open), or "unknown"
  (no seat/admission-cycle data configured yet, shown as "Seats Available").

  Requires student authentication (the requester must be logged in; the
  other friends are free text, not required to have accounts).
}
